            <ArticleTitle>[Natural history of ovary cancer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>613-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovary cancer is a disease charged of paradigms and a serious health problem. It's important to know its natural history, because has a multifactor origins, and understanding its behavior since risk factors until patient's death because metastatic disease is a challenger for oncology group. In this work we made a bibliographic, analytic review that brings up concepts related to its origin, evolution, risk factors, preclinical horizon, and clinical symptoms until the death of patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
